Blackdrift: show the app as "Blackdrift" instead of "Firefox Focus".

Why: the launcher label and in-app product name must identify this build as
Blackdrift so users can tell it apart from Mozilla Firefox Focus. app_name is a
non-translatable string defined once for the focus flavor (main/res/values),
with focusBeta/focusNightly overrides, so every locale picks up the change
without touching translations. The short onboarding name follows suit. The
user agent is not touched (upstream removed the useragent_appname token after
Firefox 150; Gecko's default mobile UA is used). Klar keeps its own name.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

diff --git a/app/src/focusBeta/res/values/app.xml b/app/src/focusBeta/res/values/app.xml
index f57980c..1e3301f 100644
--- a/app/src/focusBeta/res/values/app.xml
+++ b/app/src/focusBeta/res/values/app.xml
@@ -3,5 +3,5 @@
    - License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
    - file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. -->
 <resources>
-    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">Firefox Focus Beta</string>
+    <string name="app_name" translatable="false">Blackdrift Beta</string>
 </resources>
